WEBVTT

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.330
Is it the first time you have seen the "Blue Witch"?

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.870
Selvaria...Bles.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:27.810
Huh?!

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.400
That means...

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:33.950
Maximi...

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:38.970
You lowlifes are not permitted to speak of that name.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.540
Cease, Selvaria.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.500
Leave here, Gallian soldiers.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.920
We won't be ordered around by the likes of you!

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:50.750
Alicia!

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.770
This is Gallian territory.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:56.350
If anyone should be told to leave, it should be you,

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.630
Maximilian Gaius von Degindave.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.540
Wait.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.210
Woman, as you said, this is not Imperial territory,

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.350
but this place is not Gallian either.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:12.130
It could be said that it's Selvaria's.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.420
Yes, Valkyrian's.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.860
The Valkyrians are extinct!

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.450
They are not at all extinct.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.950
This engraving is the very evidence.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.810
It speaks of the foreboding reconquest of the world.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.720
Again...

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.340
Faldio, get low.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.400
You guys are under arrest.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.210
Selvaria.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.070
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:38.720
Wha... Stop!

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:47.860
Wait!

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:50.280
I will shoot if you go any further.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:50.880
St...

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.430
Wait!

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:17.850
Alicia, stop there.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.160
B-But...

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.750
To slash a bullet into two...

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:27.900
Chapter 8

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:27.900
Scrutinized History

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:36.850
What is it?

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.510
I thought I felt rumbling...

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.280
What? Rumbling?

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.870
Are you stupid?

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:54.910
What's going on?

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.240
Are you sure of this, Your Majesty?

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.770
I care not.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.120
The needed materials are already in our hands.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.520
Has it come?

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.150
Raze it.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.320
What? Imperials!

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.410
What size...

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.350
Sorry.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.100
This is a bombardment.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.190
Damn... So that's what they're doing.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.550
Let's leave here now before the ruin collapses.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.680
Faldio?

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.750
Go on ahead first.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.030
W-What are you saying?

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.640
What that Maximilian said sounds troubling.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.840
As soon as I understand what he meant, I'll get out.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:38.120
Damn it! They are seriously thinking of razing the Ruin.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.070
Alicia! Above you!

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.680
Faldio, take her!

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.930
Welkin!

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.090
Are you sad?

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.540
I?

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.310
Why so, Your Majesty?

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.930
I have destroyed another one of your relics.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:18.650
The only one I rely on...

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.490
Is Your Majesty.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.900
How is Fouzen doing?

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:28.950
Y-Yes!

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.680
Please change into plainer clothes, sir.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.960
Huh? What did you say?

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.920
You'll get caught if you stay in your uniform.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.940
Please hurry, sir.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.240
I understand.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:03.740
If I died here, I will be failing General Damon's expectations.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:09.220
No way! How did they know?

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.270
The industrial blocks are unharmed?

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.860
Yes, sir. Also, they reported that they have captured the enemy commander.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.200
That is not a commander.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:32.650
One who starts a fight aimlessly with no strategies or ideas

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.490
is nothing more than an imbecile who ruins the reputation of his uniform.

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:38.230
What should be done, sir?

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.470
He's an eyesore. Get rid of him.

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:42.170
Yes, sir.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.830
W-What are you doing?

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:47.090
I was under General Damon's order to...

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:04.320
Faldio!

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:15.330
Faldio!

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.420
It seems like I got cut on a boulder's edge.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.370
It's okay. It's not broken.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.260
It's only a makeshift first aid.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.140
I'm sorry.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:29.890
We should get out of here quickly.

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:33.610
It would be good it there was a hole to the outside.

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.300
It moves.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:43.440
Alicia!

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:53.090
It seems like we are able to be here thanks to the gods.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:56.010
I hope that Welkin is safe.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.790
It'll be okay, right?

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.120
This is horrible.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.430
Welkin!

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:12.270
Alicia!

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.360
Commander!

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:23.500
I'm sorry.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:27.770
Because of me, you're stuck here too.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.220
What are you saying?

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.460
You look as if it was the end of the world.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.290
It's okay.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.560
For sure, it is.

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:39.900
Welkin will find a way for us.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.130
But...

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.130
It is Welkin, you know.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:45.000
Eh?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.800
Well, isn't it?

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.860
You would know, right?

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:51.390
How weird Welkin is.

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:54.640
He does and says unexpected things.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:09:01.000
When I first met him, he was sketching carefreely when the evacuation had started too.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:07.070
Speaking of things, there is a story about Welkin when we just got into college.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:08.440
What is it?

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:15.270
There was a great beauty among the freshmen, and everyone had a bet on who would be the first person to talk to her.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:21.050
Getting to the point, archaeology is a romance.

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:22.570
Wow, that's great!

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:24.000
It seems interesting!

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.820
If it's fine, you guys should...

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:26.500
Huh?

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.490
Really? He did it again?

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:32.100
I mean, even when the professor was there, that guy... Huh?

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:37.020
Let's keep going.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:47.240
There was a guy who slipped ahead of us.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:49.730
It was Welkin.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:53.380
I was awestruck. He was totally unexpected.

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:57.640
This is even more awestriking. What do you think he said to her?

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.340
I don't know, but it was probably really impolite.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.750
Bingo.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:09.200
He said "Your facial structure is interesting, so please let me sketch it."

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:21.960
But Welkin's greatness began from there.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:25.750
Through a series of events, they became good friends.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.240
They went out?

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:29.580
Are you interested?

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.020
Of course!

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:33.370
I mean, it's not like that.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:39.770
Welkin never saw her as a woman.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:42.260
It was different from her perspective.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:43.670
Ah.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:49.450
Except, even so, she never spoke badly of Welkin.

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.700
I get how she felt.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:56.640
Welkin is strange and sometimes annoying, but...

00:10:57.290 --> 00:11:00.750
That guy has some strange charm.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.460
So, it's going to be fine!

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:09.140
What carefree logic...

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:14.810
But the truth is harsher.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:17.880
Shall we fight against the reality a little more?

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:19.290
Yes!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:20.950
Welkin!

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:21.740
Commander!

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.620
Alicia!

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:44.360
Welkin!

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:48.580
Where's the Commander?

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.390
They have been sealed inside.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:50.970
What?!

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:52.450
Alicia as well.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:55.630
It's okay. I will save those two.

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:59.390
Okay? Are you even sure you can?

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:02.380
No, I don't, but I will help them!

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.720
Welkin!

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:11.160
Hey!

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:16.110
There is no answer, huh?

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:17.920
I won't give up.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.590
That's right.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:24.020
Alicia!

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:25.430
Faldio!

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:26.300
Huh?

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.670
Alicia!

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:33.560
Hey!

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.110
Can you guys hear me!?

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:36.560
Welkin!

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.630
Yes, we can, Welkin!

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:42.990
How are things on that side?!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:44.470
I am fine!

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:46.130
Faldio has a small injury!

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:47.830
Injury?

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.560
Don't worry!

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:51.800
It's just a scratch!

00:12:56.140 --> 00:13:02.600
Well, it is going to be a race between escape and the total collapse of this place.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.340
Are you okay?

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.610
The desert night gets pretty cold.

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:10.910
I'm fine.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:14.130
I'm better off than the three looking for us outside.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:19.400
What sound is that?

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:32.800
L...

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:34.470
Liza...

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:40.360
Lizards!

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.050
Lizards?

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:46.140
They are taking shelter from the night's chill!

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:50.610
It means that there is a place that is large enough for you two to escape!

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:53.020
Are you telling us to ask the lizards?!

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:55.350
Anyway, you must look for it!

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.190
We'll do so as well!

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:07.920
A hole lizard's hearing is ten times stronger than a human's.

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:12.410
Thus, as long as they are with those two, the ruin won't collapse.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:16.010
Vice versa, if they run, then is it over for them?

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:20.060
Mr. Valt, you are pessimistic.

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:22.040
Shut up!

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:26.090
He's our Squad 1's commander.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.580
How would you even understand how I feel?

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.790
I understand.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:37.970
Faldio did not ignore that I was a Darcsen, but accepted it.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:39.420
Huh?

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:47.940
That's...

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:50.040
What is that?

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.740
It's ragnite.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.740
The ruin's walls are reflecting the sunlight.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:56.150
That's it!

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.790
Hey!

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:03.730
I am going to give you the direction and the angle!

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:06.730
There is going to be an escapable hole there!

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.270
The sun is setting. Let's hurry!

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:18.650
Is it this hole? Ah.

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:19.990
Don't look.

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:21.580
I can't guarantee anything.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:23.130
I will kick you if you do.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.800
You don't have eyes on your bottom.

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:27.000
I just know it.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.190
Understood.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.370
If I see it, you can shove me into a jail cell.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:32.380
Good.

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:39.500
Is your leg okay?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.040
Yeah, somewhat.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:49.750
Faldio!

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.720
Dead end, huh?

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.590
Alicia!

00:15:57.590 --> 00:15:59.440
Alicia, where are you?!

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.600
Welkin?

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:05.970
Alicia.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.560
Is Faldio okay as well?

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:10.070
Yeah, somehow.

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:11.860
Hold on a sec.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:14.250
It's okay. We'll save you.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:21.510
Thank you. I appreciate it.

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:24.000
There's no reason to thank me.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.220
We are comrades on the same duty.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:31.660
Let's get rid of the rocks in the way first.

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:37.390
Well then. Let us do what we can do.

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:40.690
Good grief.

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:45.640
Hurting other people? Me?

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:46.860
That's right.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:52.360
The "okay"s and "fine"s that you say are things that do not lead to results.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:53.820
Is that so?

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:59.950
However, I think the future should be decided by ourselves.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.080
For her as well?

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:07.710
Yes, it is.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:12.950
You are so bad, telling someone you rejected that it's okay.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:14.420
You're wrong on that.

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:19.090
She made the best choice, so it's okay.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:24.350
She will be happy.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:26.140
Geez.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.350
What will I do with a guy like you?

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.600
Well, it's all okay.

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:35.640
Say those lines as they were...

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:38.420
to the bride.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:42.880
Let's go!

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:51.030
Here we go!

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:59.010
Alicia. Faldio.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:17:59.950
Welkin!

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:03.780
Commander!

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:10.500
I'm so happy that you are safe.

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:17.470
Huh? Welkin, that hand...

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:19.020
Oh, oh.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:20.870
Anyhow, how was it?!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:21.700
Eh?

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:25.540
I mean the hole lizards! How did they feed their babies?

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:26.100
Huh?!

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:28.890
Do you want to know?

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:31.410
Of course I want to know!

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.000
Of course I do!

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:37.010
Man, what will I do with you?

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:39.690
Wh-What is it, Faldio?

00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:40.840
Tell me!

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:42.830
Well, what should I do?

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:43.880
Don't be pretentious!

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:45.720
It is very valuable information!

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:51.970
Commander, what's that wound?

00:18:51.970 --> 00:18:55.260
Ah, it was a little adventure.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:58.940
What the heck is this? You guys are covered in dirt!

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:01.070
On top of that, you are hurt!

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.350
We were so worried about you!

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:04.690
I'm sorry about that.

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:07.180
There is a pot full of veggies waiting.

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:10.430
If you eat it with Alicia's bread, it brings the ultimate taste.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:11.300
Really?

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.250
I'm starving!

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.560
Well then! It's time for dinner!

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:19.890
I'll leave you to first aid.

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:22.130
Also, how is Fouzen?

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.450
It's probably as you thought.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:34.850
Unfortunately, there are no stories for me to give to Your Majesty.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:40.160
It seems the Lieutenant General is in an ill mood over his victory at Fouzen.

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:41.930
Obviously, I am.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:45.040
It seems like you didn't get to meet the tank from before.

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:46.280
Hmph.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:48.580
What is that?

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:52.590
The Lieutenant General is quite fond of it at the moment.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:53.350
Ah.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:55.730
Well, with that aside,

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:58.010
is there anything from the central?

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.580
There are just a bunch of aroused vermins.

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:03.680
I see.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:08.080
Then, it seem we can enjoy things a bit more here.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.800
Yo, Rabi Jaeger here.

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:15.550
It's been a while since my country was overtaken,

00:20:15.550 --> 00:20:18.940
but this tough life isn't so bad either.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:24.290
The old enemy Gregor and the difficult Prince as well.

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:27.430
Well, I wish I could take some rest, but...

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:29.670
Next, on Valkyria Chronicles:

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:31.670
Chapter 9 - <i>Blue Witch</i>.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:33.610
If you are not tough, you can't live on.

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:35.990
If you have no dream, there is no reason to live.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:39.590
Chapter 9

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:39.590
Blue Witch

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:39.100
Good grief, being a man...
